# The built console bundle is a generated artifact — keep it byte-identical across
# platforms (no CRLF conversion) so what's committed is exactly what rust-embed bakes
# into the binary. Regenerate with `npm run build`.
dist/** -text

# Self-hosted IBM Plex woff2 (src/fonts/) — binary, and baked into both dist bundles.
# `* text=auto` at the repo root already detects these as binary; pinning it makes the
# guarantee explicit rather than dependent on content sniffing.
src/fonts/*.woff2 -text

# The Vite entry template. `* text=auto` at the repo root hands a Windows checkout
# CRLF, `npm run build` copies those bytes into dist/index.html, and `dist/** -text`
# above stores them verbatim — so the committed bundle flip-flops between CRLF and LF
# depending on which platform last rebuilt it. Pinning the source to LF makes the
# generated file deterministic instead. Leading slash on purpose: an unanchored
# `index.html` also matches dist/index.html and would re-enable text conversion on a
# file the rule above deliberately stores byte-for-byte.
/index.html text eol=lf
